CHAPTER.VERS:
I have heard many such things: Miserable comforters are all of you

          {+}
        .

I also could speak as you

          {+}
         do; If your

          {+}
         soul were in my soul's stead, I could join words together against you

          {+}
        , And shake my head at you

          {+}
        .

[But] I would strengthen you

          {+}
         with my mouth, And the solace of my lips would assuage [your

          {+}
         grief].
